# Project context

When working on this codebase, **read `docs/PROJECT_MASTER.md` first** for the full picture: motivation, product definition, current vs target, architecture, RAG/HITL flows, API surface, and documentation map.

That document contains:

- Why the platform exists and what it is (and is not)
- Stakeholder value and review workflow (operator → crew lead → MEL)
- Current architecture and the dual pipeline distinction (UI vs scheduler/CLI)
- Stack, data model, RAG pipeline, human-in-the-loop mechanics
- REST/SSE API summary and front-end behavior
- How to run and develop; adding a new report type
- Links to deeper references

For **file-by-file roles** while coding, use [docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md](docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md) (§4 repository layout and data flows).

Use PROJECT_MASTER as the single entry point so you don’t need to re-read transcripts or re-explore the repo from scratch.
